Z||000000||SilverFieroV6||09-21-2000||01:58 AM||||ok i started changing the head gaskets about a month ago, doing most of it in spare time a little here and there. well now mostly everything is back together.  But i have come up with a HUGE PROBLEM, i cant seem to figure out where all of the electric (sensor connectors) connect to.  now most of you are saying you should have tagged them, well i did but it has rained badly the past few weeks at times here, while the car was covered, the air was still damp and now all of the tags are gone.  anyone have any ideas, or know any good diagrams.  i have looked in the haines and chilton manuals and havent found anything to helpfull. <BR>thanks<BR>Sam Clark||||reg||8
Z||000001||Carrolles||09-21-2000||08:40 AM||||Is the engine in or out of the car?<P>I have the 85 Helms manual which shows all the sensor and wiring routing.  I can scan and e-mail or fax pages to you but it will take a while.  Actually I could probably fax them to you sooner because I can copy and send them from work during lunch.  At home things get pretty hectic and I have to share computer time with my wife and three college student kids.<P>Let me know how I can help.<P>Carroll||||reg||1
