Z||000005||StuGood||09-22-2000||12:46 AM||||I think in pic# 2 (.....Mvc025s), the 4-pin connector in your hand is for the IAC (idle air control), located in the throttle body.<P>Maybe you already know this, but the flat black thing (sheath?) is supposed to be tucked underneath the intermediate manifold (lower part of the split plenum), between it and the valve cover. <P>By the way, for some reason, your hands look much more lovely in the last two pics.  Must be that blue nail polish  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 09-22-2000).]||||reg||3
Z||000006||80's BOY||09-22-2000||09:30 AM||||okay....the first picture where your pointer finger is...the round connector with 3 pins goes on your oil pressure sending unit. the square plug, the one in a perfect square on the next picture goes on the tranny. let me study the others some more. i know there are better experts than me that read this but i'm just trying to help. ||||reg||14
Z||000007||80's BOY||09-22-2000||09:33 AM||||okay, on picture #3 the light colored cheesy two prong connector goes in the black one shaped just like it and should have a clip to attach it somewhere around the distributor.||||reg||1
